sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task (driver workflow) started by a Schedule, Recall swamp-owns-dependencies, R1-R3.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 14, 15 (no input read, no report step).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, maintenance is opt-in per Project.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: none · maintenance-projects Schedule
  %% kind: project.observe
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  SW-->>GW: Hourly tick succeeded<br/>maintenance-projects · :17:40
  %%> When:
  %%> - every hour at :17:40; the trigger is the one in the workflow file, and the Gateway publishes that same definition once: a `workflow.trigger.set` for a definition that serve already holds is not sent again
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the `maintenance-projects` Schedule's own run only ticks: it lists the Projects that the Swamp source configures (`projects.json`), each with its repository identity, default branch, check and the three request keys of this fire
  %%> - it reads no Gateway state, and the trigger carries no inputs
  %%> How the Gateway learns it:
  %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
  %%> - the Gateway captures result_json directly from the schedule producer `tick`, in the same history read; no reporting step forwards it
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - for each configured Project: `id`, `repository`, `default_branch`, `check` and `keys` with `routine`, `observe` and `detect`, such as `4-observe-2026-11-02T17:17`
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the schedule carries no Project or task group data. The earlier design published the Gateway's whole Project and task group snapshot (36,228 lines, 1.36 MB) as `trigger.inputs`, and every change of a Project, task group or open task wrote `serve.yaml` and registered the schedule again, 37 to 108 times an hour. The manual calls `trigger.inputs` baseline input values
  %%> - a Swamp step may call the Gateway only for `github-token` and `certificates/sign` (the Swamp shape gate), and a push of the snapshot into the Swamp datastore would repeat the churn, so the Gateway reads its own tables when it projects the fire (next step), like the other dispatch-only schedules
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no command: no person starts `project.observe` directly
  Note over GW: Select what is due<br/>own Projects · groups · open tasks
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - takes the opted-in Projects (maintenance on, GitHub App repository, default branch, task check) that the tick lists as configured with the same repository, default branch and check
  %%> - skips a Project with an open `project.detect`, `project.routine` or `project.observe` task
  %%> - picks one mode for each Project: the weekly routine first, then an observation while a group that has not ended waits on a pull request or on capacity, else the hourly inspection
  %%> - skips a mode whose key it admitted before, and takes the next mode
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - a group that ended no longer makes an observation due; the earlier selection counted any group that ever had a pull request, so a Project with one old pull request was observed every minute-key and never inspected, though an observation reads no ended group
  Note over GW: Admit observe, scope reads<br/>task #5152 · trigger: schedule
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - maintenance is on for Project 4 (`project:maintenance:enable`); it is off by default
  %%> - Project 4 reads its repository through the GitHub App, with a default branch and a task check
  %%> - no other `project.detect`, `project.routine` or `project.observe` task runs for Project 4
  %%> - the request key wasn't admitted before
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the Project and its task groups, with their watched PRs
  %%> - when there are watched PRs, mints a GitHub App token with `contents: read` and `pull_requests: read`, into the vault as `project-dependency-read-5152` (R3)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5152 recorded, kind `project.observe`, driver `workflow`, on Node 209
  %%> - no Node is a target; the work only reads GitHub
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>project-observe
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the captured Project and task groups
  %%> - the vault key names of the token, never the token
  SW->>GH: Read the watched PRs<br/>gh pr view · dependency-evidence
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the number, state and head of each watched pull request of Project 4
  %%> How:
  %%> - `gh` reads the token with `vault.get`
  Note over SW: Refresh the findings index<br/>orbit-gateway refresh
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - links the PR states to the Project's last findings in Swamp data
  %%> - names task groups that waited for capacity and can start now
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the PR observations and the groups that can resume, as this step's output, which the Gateway reads from the terminal result
  alt observation done
    GH-->>SW: PR #57 merged
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - each PR's state: open, closed or merged
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · observations
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event
    Note over GW: Record PR states<br/>settle group #812 · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task group #812 records PR #57 as merged
    %%> - a maintenance group whose PR merged or closed moves to settling; the Gateway admits `tasks.maintenance_finish` to remove its workspace
    %%> - a group that waited for capacity gets `tasks.provision`
    %%> - task #5152 succeeds
    %%> Not changed:
    %%> - a group whose watched PR or settings changed after capture
  else a read fails
    GH--xSW: token refused, API error
    %%> When:
    %%> - GitHub refuses the token or doesn't answer
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>groups unchanged · next hour
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5152 fails; no task group changes
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the next hourly fire admits a new observe task with a new key
  end
